    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***SECOND FLOOR / 2 BED 1 BATH SPACIOUS APARTMENT / UNDERGROUND ALLOCATED  PARKING SPACE / BALCONY / B RATED GREEN MORTGAGE / SECURE GATED DEVELOPMENT / PRIME LOCATION / EXCELLENT TRANSPORT LINKS***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to present to the market Apartment 12, Richmond Hall, Drumcondra, Dublin 3.\r\n\r\nThis stunning two-bedroom apartment is located on the second floor of this sought-after development and presents as a bright and spacious apartment with a thoughtfully considered floor plan of well-appointed accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe entrance hall with storage room and hot press gives access to the bright open-plan living/dining room with beautiful semi solid engineered walnut flooring that leads to a sizeable balcony with panoramic city views. This home has Aluwood windows and the balcony door has \"Tilt and Turn\" capability. The open-plan kitchen boasts an array of cream and beech wall and floor kitchen units with attractive Quartz countertop & tiled back splash and floor, giving the kitchen a luxurious and elegant feel. Both double bedrooms feature fitted wardrobes and carpet flooring. A fully tiled bathroom with bath, over bath shower, basin and W.C. completes the accommodation.\r\n\r\nRichmond Hall is ideally located in a mature gated development on Richmond Road, only a moment’s stroll from Fairview and Drumcondra. The location is second to none, situated just to the north east of Dublin's city centre, making it a convenient place to live for those who work or study in the city. The neighbourhood offers a mix of housing types, including apartments, houses and period-style homes. It attracts a diverse range of residents, from young to families and retirees. One of the notable features of the area is Fairview Park, a spacious public park with green lawns, walking paths, and a playground. It provides a fantastic recreational space for residents and visitors and holds concerts in the summer months.  \r\n\r\nFairview Strand is a road that runs along the coastline to Clontarf, offering scenic views of Dublin Bay. It is a popular spot for walking and enjoying the waterfront. Fairview has a range of amenities, including shops, supermarkets, restaurants, cafes & gyms. Residents have easy access to essential services and dining options. The neighbourhood is well connected to Dublin's public transportation network. It has several bus routes serving the area, providing convenient access to the city centre and surrounding areas. Fairview has an active and engaged community, with local groups and initiatives that contribute to the area's vibrancy and sense of community. \r\n\r\nThere are several schools and educational institutions in and around Fairview & Drumcondra, making it a great catchment area for families with children. The location is within striking distance of industry and enterprise centres of business including the IFSC, Eastpoint Business Park, The Beckett Building and Grand Canal Dock.\r\n\r\nNearby, Croke Park Stadium, one of Ireland's most iconic sporting venues, hosts various events and matches, including Gaelic games and concerts. It's a popular destination for sports enthusiasts and concertgoers.\r\n\r\nRichmond Road is a well-rounded neighbourhood offering a mix of residential options, green spaces, amenities, and accessibility to Dublin's city centre. Its location and community spirit make it an attractive place to call home for a diverse range of residents.\r\n\r\nApartment 12, Richmond Hall will surely prove popular with first-time buyers, downsizers or those looking for a city pad. To appreciate all that this superb property has to offer, viewing is highly recommended and available through KELLY BRADSHAW."
      },
